-- title:
--   Unit Katz independence elements for Drinfeld Γ(q)-bases
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be an odd prime, $A_0$ a commutative ring, and $\mathcal G$ a family of group laws over $A_0$: for every $A_0$-algebra $T$ and every projective Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$ with invertible discriminant, a relative group law on the projective model of $W$. Assume $\mathcal G$ is chord–tangent (each member admits a points-evaluation datum `IsPointsEval`) and has origin identity (the identity section of each member is cut out on the origin chart by a ring homomorphism killing $xOverY$ and $zOverY$). Let $\mathcal T$ be a level transport for $(\mathcal G,q)$ whose base-change and variable-change maps carry the two sections of a pair to the expected ones (`IsSectionTransport`). Let $T$ be an $A_0$-algebra in which $q$ is invertible, $E$ a Weierstrass curve over $T$, and $x$ a raw Drinfeld pair over $T$ — a projective Weierstrass curve $x.\mathrm{curve}$ with sections $P,Q$ — such that $x.\mathrm{curve}$ is the projective model of $E$, its discriminant is a unit, and $(P,Q)$ is a Drinfeld basis of the $q$-torsion, i.e. the basis divisor of $(P,Q)$ equals the $q$-torsion ideal. Suppose $P$ passes through the affine point $(x_P,y_P)$ and $Q$ through $(x_Q,y_Q)$, in the sense that the $Z$-chart of $x.\mathrm{curve}$ admits a section homomorphism to $T$ realising $P$ (resp. $Q$) with affine coordinates those values. Then both independence elements $\prod_{a=1}^{(q-1)/2}\bigl(x_Q\,\Psi_a^2(x_P)-\Phi_a(x_P)\bigr)$ and $\prod_{a=1}^{(q-1)/2}\bigl(x_P\,\Psi_a^2(x_Q)-\Phi_a(x_Q)\bigr)$ are units of $T$.
--
--   The Katz–Mazur comparison between a Drinfeld basis of $E[q]$ and the naive independence condition at invertible level: the vanishing locus of the independence element records where one of the two points lies in the cyclic subgroup generated by the other, so invertibility expresses independence over every residue field of the base. It supplies the unit-independence data required by the $\Gamma(q)$-level moduli package, and is used in the computations of determinants of relabelling matrices and of the Weil pairing for Drinfeld bases.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_DrinfeldGlobal_RawDrinfeldPair_IsLevel_isUnit_indepElt_of_isSectionThrough.lean

